<title>FRANCE: N.France grain may still recover from drought - ONIC.</title>
<headline>N.France grain may still recover from drought - ONIC.</headline>
<dateline>ROUEN, France 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain crops in the main producing regions of northern France may still recover from a three-month drought, but the situation in the south looks worse, the head of the national grain office ONIC said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;France is suffering from drought. The rain of the last days has helped the situation but is insufficient to make up for ground lost over the last months. The situation seems already compromised in the southern part (of the country) but is not irreversible for the large grain basin of the north,&quot; director general Alain Moulinier told a grain conference in the port city of Rouen.</p>
<p>Last week France's largest farm union, the FNSEA, said the drought had done irreversible harm to winter grain crops.</p>
